a","assessments":[5]},"cod-35MPS9581_1":{"kind":"settlement","name":"Cinjira","alt_names":"Buhamba; Mugeri","lat":-2.88531,"lon":28.75525,"population":5769,"pop_source":"GRID3 COD population v4.4 (100 m)","building_count":1632,"extent_type":"Small Settlement Area","grid3_extent_id":"35MPS9581_1","adm1_pcode":"CD62","adm2_pcode":"CD6212","adm3_pcode":"CD621204","health_zone":"Mwana","health_area":"Buhamba","name_source":"grid3_names:inside","assessments":[5]},"cod-35MPS9682_1":{"kind":"settlement","name":"Buhuka","lat":-2.87512,"lon":28.7679,"population":1507,"pop_source":"GRID3 COD population v4.4 (100 m)","building_count":507,"extent_type":"Small Settlement Area","grid3_extent_id":"35MPS9682_1","adm1_pcode":"CD62","adm2_pcode":"CD6212","adm3_pcode":"CD621204","health_zone":"Mwana","health_area":"Buhamba","name_source":"grid3_names:inside","assessments":[5]}},"assessments":[{"controller_id":"cod-wazalendo","sovereign_id":"cod","status":"unclear","confidence":"low","basis":"inference","as_of":"2026-10-01","zone":"Katonga (Mulombozi area, Itombwe lowlands toward Kitutu)","evidence":"Remote area of Itombwe secteur west of the plateaux in the Mwenga health zone; Mai-Mai/Wazalendo groups are the reported armed actors; no specific information.","unit":"CD6212-mwenga","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","presence":[{"entity_id":"twirwaneho","role":"raiding"}],"source_ids":[94]},{"controller_id":"twirwaneho","sovereign_id":"twirwaneho","status":"dominant","confidence":"low","basis":"area_report","as_of":"2026-10-01","since":"2025-02","zone":"Itombwe secteur high plateaux / Minembwe health zone and Bijojo: Minembwe Centre, Mikenge, Kilulwe, Magandi","evidence":"Twirwaneho, allied to AFC/M23, took Minembwe after FARDC withdrew in February 2025 and dominates the Banyamulenge high plateaux including Mikenge and Bijojo, while Mai-Mai/Wazalendo groups contest the surrounding forest and lowlands.","unit":"CD6212-mwenga","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","presence":[{"entity_id":"afc-m23-arc","role":"allied"},{"entity_id":"cod-wazalendo","role":"contesting"}],"source_ids":[94,149]},{"controller_id":"afc-m23-arc","sovereign_id":"afc-m23","status":"contested","confidence":"low","basis":"inference","as_of":"2026-10-01","since":"2025","zone":"RN2 corridor between Kaziba/Luhwindja and Mwenga centre: Kilungutwe, Kangola, Kalama, Kasika, Kadita, Muhuzi","evidence":"The Bukavu–Mwenga–Kamituga road (RN2) east of Mwenga centre has been a frontline between M23 pushing south-west from Walungu/Kaziba and Wazalendo/FARDC defending Mwenga since 2025; control of individual villages has shifted repeatedly. Reviewer: attribution of these RN2 villages to M23 rather than Wazalendo/FARDC is unverified; treat as a placeholder for the frontline.","unit":"CD6212-mwenga","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","presence":[{"entity_id":"cod-fardc","role":"contesting"},{"entity_id":"cod-wazalendo","role":"contesting"}],"source_ids":[100,149]},{"controller_id":"cod-wazalendo","sovereign_id":"cod","status":"dominant","confidence":"low","basis":"inference","as_of":"2026-10-01","since":"2025-02","zone":"Mwenga centre (Kitamba) and the Mwenga health zone west of Kasika: Kalambi, Kigezi, Kitumba, Iganda, Butezi, Muzombo, Kibanda, Kananda","evidence":"The territorial seat remained in the government camp after February 2025; FARDC units retreating from Bukavu/Walungu regrouped toward Mwenga and Kamituga, where Mai-Mai/Wazalendo groups became the main armed force with their own roadblocks and taxation. Specific group not determined.","unit":"CD6212-mwenga","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","presence":[{"entity_id":"cod-fardc","role":"allied"},{"entity_id":"cod-pnc","role":"present"},{"entity_id":"afc-m23-arc","role":"raiding"}],"source_ids":[94,100]},{"controller_id":"raia-mutomboki","sovereign_id":"raia-mutomboki","status":"dominant","confidence":"low","basis":"area_report","as_of":"2026-10-01","zone":"Kitutu secteur / Kitutu health zone (Kabisa, Mission, Kabilongo, Katimbo, Kakemenge, Lubimbi, Kitutu–Mapale/Makalanga mining area, Matebo, Kasola, Mitembu)","evidence":"Kitutu borders Shabunda and has long hosted Raia Mutomboki/Mai-Mai factions taxing gold sites, now nominally Wazalendo; state presence limited to small posts in larger centres.","unit":"CD6212-mwenga","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","presence":[{"entity_id":"cod-fardc","role":"present"},{"entity_id":"cod-pnc","role":"present"}],"source_ids":[94]},{"controller_id":"afc-m23-arc","sovereign_id":"afc-m23","status":"dominant","confidence":"low","basis":"inference","as_of":"2026-10-01","since":"2025-02","zone":"Luhwindja chefferie / Mwana health zone (Mwana–Twangiza area and its neighbourhoods, Buhamba, Cinjira, Buhuka) and Kimalanjala area east of Kilungutwe","evidence":"Luhwindja and the Twangiza mining area adjoin M23-held Walungu/Kaziba and were reported occupied by AFC/M23 after the February 2025 fall of Bukavu; Wazalendo raids from Burhinyi and western hills continued. No known recapture through the reference date. Reviewer: basis changed from area_report to inference because no dated report on Luhwindja/Twangiza could be consulted; the cited sources are generic index pages.","unit":"CD6212-mwenga","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","presence":[{"entity_id":"cod-wazalendo","role":"raiding"}],"source_ids":[100,149,159]},{"controller_id":"cod-wazalendo","sovereign_id":"cod","status":"dominant","confidence":"low","basis":"inference","as_of":"2026-10-01","since":"2025-02","zone":"Kamituga mining city (all neighbourhoods) and Kamituga health zone (Ngambo, Mangele, Lubigi Tongo, Biza, Kabeba, Kabumba, Musumba, Bungalama, Kankanga)","evidence":"Kamituga stayed outside M23 control; after the 2025 collapse of the eastern front FARDC remnants and Wazalendo/Mai-Mai groups (incl. Raia Mutomboki elements) dominate the town and mining sites, with reported indiscipline, extortion and clashes; PNC and administration remain present.","unit":"CD6212-mwenga","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","presence":[{"entity_id":"cod-fardc","role":"allied"},{"entity_id":"cod-pnc","role":"present"},{"entity_id":"raia-mutomboki","role":"present"}],"source_ids":[94,100]}],"sources":{"94":{"url":"https://kivusecurity.org/","title":"Kivu Security Tracker (Ituri/Irumu incident data)","publisher":"Congo Research Group / Human Rights Watch"},"149":{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/M23_campaign_(2022%E2%80%93present)","title":"M23 campaign (2022–present)","publisher":"Wikipedia"},"100":{"url":"https://www.radiookapi.net/","title":"Radio Okapi – Ituri news (background)","publisher":"Radio Okapi"},"159":{"url":"https://www.un.org/securitycouncil/sanctions/1533/work-and-mandate/expert-reports","title":"UN Group of Experts on the DRC final reports (2019-2025): CNPSC/Yakutumba, Twirwaneho and Mai-Mai in Fizi, Itombwe and Minembwe","publisher":"United Nations Security Council","date":"2025-06-01"}},"units":{"CD6212-mwenga":"Mwenga territory sits on the south-western edge of the AFC/M23 zone in Sud-Kivu. The eastern part (Luhwindja chefferie / Mwana health zone with Twangiza) is assessed as held by M23 since its February 2025 advance from Bukavu and Walungu, and the RN2 corridor toward Mwenga centre (Kilungutwe–Kasika) as a contested frontline. Mwenga centre, Kamituga and the Kitutu gold area remain in the government camp but are dominated by Wazalendo/Mai-Mai and Raia Mutomboki groups alongside weakened FARDC and PNC. The Itombwe high plateaux (Minembwe, Mikenge, Bijojo) are held by M23-allied Twirwaneho since February 2025. Live web research was unavailable for this unit (search budget exhausted, news/UN sites blocked by the egress proxy), so all zones are low-confidence inferences from background knowledge up to mid-2026. Review (2026-10-01): the reviewer could not run independent web research either (search budget exhausted; Bing, Google, DuckDuckGo and ReliefWeb blocked by the egress proxy), so zones were checked only for internal and geographic consistency with the neighbouring Walungu, Shabunda, Uvira and Fizi assessments; no controller changes were made, the Luhwindja zone basis was lowered to inference and the RN2 frontline attribution flagged as unverified."}}